Privacy Policy

Last updated: 15-Jan-26

BlockApp is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how your personal information is collected, used, and disclosed by BlockApp.

By accessing or using our Service, you signify that you have read, understood, and agree to our collection, storage, use, and disclosure of your personal information as described in this Privacy Policy and our Terms of Service.

1. Information We Collect and How We Use It

Our application operates primarily as an offline utility. We do not collect personal data to sell to third parties. However, to function as an App Locker, the app requires access to specific sensitive data on your device.

A. App Usage Statistics (Critical)

To perform its core function (locking apps), the app uses the PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS permission.

What we access: The app monitors the "current foreground package" to detect when you open an app (e.g., WhatsApp, Gallery).

How we use it: This data is processed instantly and locally on your device to determine if the opened app matches a blocked app in your settings.

Data Retention: This data is NOT stored, NOT transmitted to any server, and NOT shared with third parties. It is ephemeral and exists only in the device's temporary memory (RAM) for milliseconds to trigger the lock screen.

B. Installed Application Inventory

To allow you to select which apps to lock, we use the QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES permission.

What we access: The list of applications installed on your device (App Names and Package Names).

How we use it: To display a list within the app so you can select which ones to protect.

Data Retention: The list of "Locked Apps" is stored locally on your device in SharedPreferences. It is never uploaded to any external server.

C. Passwords and Biometrics

PIN/Password: The PIN you create is stored locally on your device. We do not have access to your PIN, and we cannot recover it if lost.

Biometrics (Fingerprint): We use the standard Android Biometric API. The app does not store your fingerprint data; it simply asks the Android System to verify your identity. The result (Success/Fail) is returned to the app.

2. Permissions

We request the following permissions to ensure the app functions correctly:

Usage Access: To detect when a locked app is launched.

Display Over Other Apps (Overlay): To show the Lock Screen (PIN/Fingerprint) over the app you are trying to open.

Foreground Service: To ensure the lock monitoring service runs reliably in the background without being killed by the system.

Post Notifications: To display a persistent notification required by the Android System for background monitoring.

3. Data Safety and Third-Party Services

We do not transmit your personal data to any external servers. The app functions 100% offline regarding your personal app usage data.

However, the app may use third-party services that may collect information used to identify you (e.g., for crash reporting or strictly necessary infrastructure).

